 "derivation_rule": "Pre-registered before any measurement of this scene: the 18 files fixed by fixtures/public/group-comparison/ds6a-manifest.json (Codex, PR #99): for Untreated and ActD1, the first three files of each replicate Rep1–Rep3 in file-name order. Each plane is cropped to 640 x 640 pixels (for the published seed size) by crop_rule (see derivation_amendment). Channels: Hoechst (c3), NPM1 (c1), 5-EU (c2). No field is selected or removed by its count, size or signal. Objects are removed only by the fragment review (scenario.fragment_review, see derivation_amendment): an object whose nucleolus is not established and whose area is below 0.6 of its field's median nuclear area. The rule reads area only; it does not test contact with the crop border.",
 "crop_rule": {
  "kind": "nuclear-window",
  "size": [
   640,
   640
  ],
  "step": 64,
  "basis": "The 640 x 640 window, on a 64-pixel grid, holding the most Hoechst pixels above the plane's Otsu threshold; ties go to the window nearest the centre. Only the nuclear channel is read, never NPM1 or 5-EU (cytellect_showcase.build.nuclear_window)."
 },
 "derivation_amendment": "Amended after the first scenario run, before any nucleolar or 5-EU value was read: the pre-registered centre crops held 0-2 nuclei in four of the 18 fields (Rep1 ActD file 52, Rep2 ActD file 112, Rep3 Untreated files 121 and 122); in Rep3 Untreated file 122 the crop held no nucleus and StarDist returned 51 objects in the cytoplasm, which left the field's nucleolar compartments unresolved and stopped the build. The crop position is now chosen per field from the nuclear stain alone (crop_rule). The 18 files, channels, groups, runs and every later rule are unchanged; no field is removed. Second amendment, after the re-cropped scenario run and before any nucleolar or 5-EU value was read: three objects had no established nucleolus (all three lay at the crop border on the overlay; the rule itself reads area only) (152, 2079 and 3222 px; 0.03, 0.49 and 0.58 of their field's median nuclear area), which leaves those fields' compartments unresolved. The build's existing fragment review (scenario.fragment_review, used by the earlier public demo of this dataset) is applied: an unresolved object smaller than 0.6 of its field's median nuclear area is deleted from the nuclei, as the workspace's region deletion does, and listed in manifest.json (scenario.fragment_review); any larger unresolved nucleus stops the build.",
 "selection": {
  "rule": "first three files per replicate and condition in file-name order; crop by crop_rule"
 },
